@startuml verification-ci-flow
' ============================================================================
' verification-ci-flow — what the formal-correspondence harness runs.
'
' scripts/verify-formal-correspondence.sh is the single CI-practical entry
' point. Its DEFAULT (always-on) body runs four checks in series; three further
' stages are ENV-GATED, each its own (independently-scheduled) CI job in
' .github/workflows/ci.yml. They are grouped in one partition below for
' readability — in CI they run as separate, parallel jobs, not in sequence:
'   * formal-correspondence  — default body (no env flags)         [every push]
'   * formal-miri            — RUN_MIRI=1                            [every push]
'   * formal-io-uring        — RUN_IO_URING=1                        [every push]
'   * formal-tlc             — RUN_TLC=1        [schedule / workflow_dispatch only]
'
' Grounded in formal-verification/README.md ("End-to-End Correspondence Check")
' and .github/workflows/ci.yml.
'
' Color key (verification palette — task spec):
'   green #C8E6C9 = Rocq theorem-proving stage
'   blue  #BBDEFB = TLA+/TLC model-checking stage
'   amber #FFE0B2 = CI gate / control (harness entry, unsafe set-equality gate)
'   red   #FFCDD2 = a failing outcome (fail-closed)
'   grey  #ECEFF1 = Rust correspondence tests / terminal
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
  DiamondBorderColor #EF6C00
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFE0B2
}

title Formal-correspondence harness — scripts/verify-formal-correspondence.sh

start
#FFE0B2:**verify-formal-correspondence.sh**\n(CI-practical entry point);

partition "Default body — always run (job: formal-correspondence)" {
  #ECEFF1:**Rust correspondence tests**\ncargo test trace tests:\nBTreeMap/reference vs trie, WAL crash-prefix,\nlock-free histories, dictionary laws;
  if (all trace tests pass?) then (yes)
  else (no)
    #FFCDD2:**fail closed** — code diverged from a spec;
    stop
  endif

  #C8E6C9:**Rocq proof build** — `cd rocq && make`\n(69 .v / 1,301 props; rejects any\nAdmitted / Axiom / Parameter);
  if (make succeeds, 0 escape hatches?) then (yes)
  else (no)
    #FFCDD2:**fail closed** — a proof broke;
    stop
  endif

  #BBDEFB:**TLA⁺ SANY parse** — tla2sany on the focused\n.tla models (syntax + semantic check, no TLC);
  if (all 55 modules parse?) then (yes)
  else (no)
    #FFCDD2:**fail closed** — a spec is malformed;
    stop
  endif

  #FFE0B2:**unsafe-inventory set-equality gate**\nverify-unsafe-boundary-inventory.sh:\nlive src/**/*.rs `unsafe`  ≡  UNSAFE_INVENTORY.tsv (43)\n→ every tag in UNSAFE_CONTRACTS.tsv (31) w/ valid coverage+status;
  if (inventory ≡ live, contracts valid?) then (yes)
  else (no)
    #FFCDD2:**fail closed** — undocumented / drifted `unsafe`;
    stop
  endif
}

' --- Env-gated optional stages (each its own CI job; run in parallel in CI) --
partition "Optional env-gated stages — each a separate CI job, run independently" {
  #BBDEFB:**RUN_MIRI=1**  (job: formal-miri)\n**Miri** under FORMAL_MIRI_TOOLCHAIN=nightly —\nstrict-provenance UB checks: raw child ownership,\nswizzled extraction, SwizzledPtr state transitions,\nbuffer-fixed lifetime;
  #BBDEFB:**RUN_IO_URING=1**  (job: formal-io-uring)\n**io_uring storage checks** (Linux host):\nrange rejection, fixed-buffer registration lifetime,\nSQE/CQE completion lifecycle;
  #BBDEFB:**RUN_TLC=1**  (job: formal-tlc — schedule / dispatch only)\n**TLC model checking** of the bounded models —\nexhaustive reachable-state enumeration,\n0 invariant/temporal violations;
}

#C8E6C9:**all green** — proofs, models, code, and the\n`unsafe` boundary agree;
stop

legend right
| Color | Stage |
|<#ECEFF1>| Rust correspondence tests |
|<#C8E6C9>| Rocq theorem proving |
|<#BBDEFB>| TLA⁺ / TLC model checking |
|<#FFE0B2>| CI gate / control |
|<#FFCDD2>| fail-closed outcome |
endlegend
@enduml
